  {
    "id": "PSF-018397",
    "ref": "pge:7245-lz",
    "name": "Wadi Mujib - South face Landing",
    "lat": 31.4664,
    "lon": 35.7794,
    "wind": {},
    "altitude": 445.0,
    "sources": {
      "pge": "7245-lz"
    },
    "primary": "pge",
    "role": "landing",
    "tow": false,
    "group": [
      "pge:7245"
    ],
    "notes": "Best is to land on top, easy if you have the altitude for it.\r\nIf you have to land down, there is a small place near a track 200m down the viewpoint but it is small and technical. My advice is to go check before flying and find a place that you think is good for you.\r\n(you can also try to go see down in the wadi to the East (to the dam), if you can find a suitable place to land close to the road.)",
    "url": "https://www.paraglidingearth.com/?site=7245"
  },
  {
